eending.com/blog/raspberry-picking-striptease-1996/amp"}, {"title": "New Immissions/Updates:", "url": "https://wikipedia2007.classicistranieri.com/s/t/r/Striptease_%28film%29.html"}]}, "Yes, the 1996 film *Striptease* is based on Carl Hiaasen's novel. The results agree on the basic facts:\n\n- **Source and plot:** Based on Carl Hiaasen's 1993 best-selling novel of the same name, the film centers on an FBI secretary-turned-stripper who becomes involved in both a child-custody dispute and corrupt politics.\n- **Production:** Andrew Bergman wrote, produced, and directed the film, which starred Demi Moore, Armand Assante, Ving Rhames, Robert Patrick and Burt Reynolds. The AFI catalog lists the literary source as the book Strip Tease by Carl Hiaasen (New York, 1993).\n- **Faithfulness to the novel:** One critic said the novel's plot is \"quite faithfully followed\" by the screenplay. Bergman said Hiaasen loved the movie and thought it was really, really true to the book. A separate blog post also reports that Hiaasen considered it a faithful adaptation.\n- **Reception:** Critics were harsh. One review calls the film a sinking production that the Everglades would swallow, and the film won several Golden Raspberry Awards, including Worst Picture of 1996 according to a Wikipedia mirror.\n\nSources note a few small differences in details like runtime (111 to 117 minutes), which likely reflect different cuts or listings."], "durationSeconds": 5.956411459000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01DbvoBsGM3jaersUUSQmMiX", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
